.TH "cbor::diagnostic_notation" "3" "2026-10-31" "mbedded\-cbor 0.9.0" "mbedded\-cbor"
.SH NAME
cbor::diagnostic_notation \- prints an item as diagnostic notation (RFC 8949 section 8)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]<cbor/cbor.hpp>\f[R]
.EE
.IP
.EX
std::expected<std::string, error> diagnostic_notation(std::string_view encoded);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Gives the text of the item in \f[CR]encoded\f[R] in the diagnostic
notation of RFC 8949 section 8.
A head that is not in preferred form carries its encoding indicator, for
example \f[CR]1_0\f[R].
Indefinite length is printed, for example \f[CR][_ 1]\f[R].
A tag is printed as its number and its content; tag 29 is not resolved.
.PP
\f[CR]encoded\f[R] holds exactly one item.
The call does not check tag content, UTF\-8 or duplicate keys.
.SH ERRORS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R]: the bytes end before the item ends.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]syntax_error\f[R]: a head is not well\-formed, a chunk of an
indefinite string has the wrong type, or bytes follow the item.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]nesting_depth_exceeded\f[R]: the item is deeper than
limits\f[CR]::nesting_depth\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]string_length_exceeded\f[R],
\f[CR]container_elements_exceeded\f[R]: a limit is set and the item goes
past it.
.SH NOTES
O(n).
The string allocates; its size is O(n).
The stack is O(d), d the nesting depth.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// bytes: {\(dqa\(dq: [1, 2.5, h\(aq01\(aq]}\f[R]
cbor::diagnostic_notation(bytes);   \f[I]// \(dq{\(rs\(dqa\(rs\(dq: [1, 2.5, h\(aq01\(aq]}\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// bytes: 9f 01 ff\f[R]
cbor::diagnostic_notation(bytes);   \f[I]// \(dq[_ 1]\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// bytes: 01 02\f[R]
cbor::diagnostic_notation(bytes);   \f[I]// syntax_error\f[R]
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
mbedded\-cbor(3), cbor::lazy(3), cbor::at_path(3), cbor::item(3), cbor::structs(3), cbor::schema(3), cbor::ref(3), cbor::item_size(3), cbor::sequence(3), cbor::sequence_reader(3), cbor::error(3)
